Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the BSS section being cleared before the initrd was moved to a safe location. During decompression, the BSS section could overlap with the initrd, leading to corruption of the initrd contents depending on the sizes of the compressed kernel and the BSS section. This overlap could occur if the bootloader placed the initrd in a location that conflicted with the BSS area, resulting in data loss or corruption.

